NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1049,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,3,2,4,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.0868,"rank":0.1503,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV002502","role":"target","render":{"description":"A pool in which a mill sank; a pool in which hay wagons vanished and in which a coach disappears after a voice in the water asked where the man is, for the time has come. A will-o'-the-wisp above the pool means that someone will drown or that a house will be built.","place":null,"prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/45349"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV002004","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A light above a pool is seen as an omen of an accident. Later a boy drowns there who had got drunk out of grief at being rejected by a girl.","place":"Mussel","prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43322","original":"Achter de boerderij van mijn broer in Mussel was in het \"oal daip\" - de Mussel A - een diepe kolk. Zw. Tuin ziet op een avond boven die kolk een licht branden. Ze vermoedt een komend ongeluk. En dit komt.\n'n Poos later is er een feest. Een jonge man - G.D. - vraagt een meisje, of ze 's avonds met hem uit wil. Ze heeft er geen zin in. \nVan verdriet drinkt hij zich dronken.\nLater heeft 't kind spijt van haar weigering, want D. wordt de andere dag dood uit de kolk gehaald.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.955,7.03889]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV006902","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Prediction that something will happen by a canal; people with a light were seen crossing a road. Later a drowned boy was carried home along that path in the evening.","place":"Vriescheloo","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43572","original":"Veurloop.\nOabram zag nog meer. Wazzen es n poar jongelu, dei zoln troun-n. \nToun de haile boudel veurmekoar was, woln ze de meubels koopn in Winschootn. t Wicht gung dr op of en de jong zol den in Winschootn bie heur koom-m. Hai bedochde zuk en verdronk zuk in n wieke.  \nMoar, en hier gait mie t om, oal Oabram har al joarn van te veurn zegd:“Doar gunders bie de wieke gebeurt nog es n keer wat. Ik zai dr mensn deur t veld trekn; langs dei loane goan ze en koom-m bie dei boerderij oet. Misschain verdrinkt dr wel aine. Ik zai ook, dat ze n lichie bie zuk hebben.” \nEn net zo is t gebeurd. Bie oavend hebben ze de jong langs t zulfde pad van de wieke noar hoes brocht.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.06833,7.11389]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"WEV007506","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A prediction that someone will drown in a canal within a day comes true.","place":"Veelerveen","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44134","original":"Toun ze mit t knoal aan t groaven wazzen, moz dr in t leste nog n dam deurstookn wordn.\nWazzen verschaiden manlu bie aan t waark.\nToun kwam dr aine langs, bleef n rukje stoan en zee: \n\"Joa, 't is n mooi knoal worn; t is allaind zo jammer, dat dr binnen vaarntwintig uur ain in verdrinkn mout.\"\n\"Och, doe hest altied wat\", zeden de keerls, en zai smeetn hom mit n schop vol zaand noar de kop.\nMoar kiek, d ander dag, t luip teegn twaalf uur en de mensn woln gau eetn, zee dr n seldoat teegn zien mouder:\n\"Ik goa eerst nog eevn zwemmen heur, veur t eetn.\"\n\"Och, jong, blief hier toch\", zee ze, t is muide nait meer weerd.\"\nHai gung toch hen, mor is best verdronkn.\n\nAal dizze vertelsels binnen woar.\nIk heb ze zulf beleefd.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.05583,7.12778]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Mussel.","Find Barlage on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[53.0125,7.05556],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Barlage"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1447,"rank":0.2897,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ046312","role":"member","render":{"description":"Never run in the middle of the road at night: a funeral procession may pass.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24424","original":"Wy woarden altyd warskôge: rin noait midden op 'e wei by joun of by nacht, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje passeare.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ102104","role":"member","render":{"description":"Some people had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. You should never run in the middle of the road at night.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37102","original":"Yn 'e Harkema en yn Stiensgea ha 'k wol guon kend dy't nachts fan bêd moesten om lykstaesjes to sjen.\nMen moest nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ052415","role":"member","render":{"description":"The narrator tells of two men who often saw funeral processions. You must never walk in the middle of the road, because an invisible funeral procession can drive you off the road.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25234","original":"Douwe Stavasius fan Grinzer Pein seach lykstaesjes.\nBoardzer Bruining fan Boelensloane ek. Dy leeft noch.\nMen mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje oankomme, sûnder dat men it sjocht. Dan wurde jo fan 'e wei ôfsmiten.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"HOL003326","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"In the evening someone is jumped by a witch or werewolf.","place":"Tiel","prov":"Gld.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210358","original":"Een ander verhaal uit de Nude: Iemand moest 's avonds de paarden naar de wei brengen. Toen gebeurde het eens, dat hem een \"teuverheks\" of een \"weerwolf\" op de rug sprong.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:3"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Tiel belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.1253,"rank":0.3054,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ110507","role":"omen","render":{"description":"If seven black rooks fly over the house, a death is coming. It is an omen.","place":"Kootstertille","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29560","original":"As der sawn swarte roeken oer 't hûs hinne fleagen, kaem der yn dat hûs in deaden.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ111804","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A man born with a caul is often driven out of bed at night to have a vision. At the time of the Spanish flu (November 1918) the clairvoyant sees as many as seven funeral processions at once.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29954","original":"Bontsje Knjillis wie algemien bikend. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren, dat wist elkenien. Nachts moest er faek út bêd wei om hwat to sjen. Dy't dat hat, kin net lizzen bliuwe. Dat mei nou ienkear net.\nOp in kear wie Bontsje Knjillis bot fan 'e wize. Doe hied er wol sawn lykstaesjes tagelyk sjoen. Dat wie yn 'e tiid fan 'e Spaenske gryp (novimber 1918).","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"GENDT168","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A man visits a fortune teller who shows him a photo of his future wife and has him draw seven cards, from which she concludes that he will later work with sharp objects. Both come true.","place":"Gendt","prov":"Gld.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"M.H.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/50192","original":"Toe ik bé’j Veenhuus in Huse as smidsknechje diende, was er nog ’n knech bé’j die smid. Op ’n keer sproke we samen af um es nor ’n woarzegster in Oarem te goan. ’t Was alleen mar uut spitsboeveré’j. Toe we bé’j de vrouw kwame, liet ze mien ers ’n foto zien. En ze zèj: “Hier, die foto is van een meisje, waar je later mee zult trouwen”. Ik keek er heel goed nor. Lotter kreeg ik verkering. En ik zag drek al bé’j de erste kennismaking, dat ’t de eigeste dern was, die ’k bé’j de woarzegster opte foto had gezien. En ik bun er mè getrouwd en gelukkig mè gewes. ’t Was dus wel uutgekomme. Dornoa noom de vrouw ’n stel koarte. Ik mos er zeuve uuttrekke. Ik deej ’t. En de vrouw noom ze over. …","lang":"Gendt dialect (Achterhoek)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","7 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":7},"on_success":{"chime":7,"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.6258,"rank":0.0,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"HOL000404","role":"variant","render":{"description":"Seeing a witte juffer (white lady); playing at being a witte juffer with a white sheet around oneself.","place":"Ingen","prov":"Gld.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209537","original":"Witte vrouwen . Bij de pas (aanplant van wilgen of populieren met onderhout van elzen en essen) (lag dicht bij de woning van de zegslieden) zag men soms een witte gedaante lopen. Maar sommigen geloofden niet aan de witte juffer, zo werd Han Briene er van verdacht, dat hij soms de kinderen bang wilde maken door voor witte juffer te spelen (hij deed zich dan een laken om) Enige jongens wilden met Jas Gaosbeek, een niet volwaardige zoon van een bakker, een grap uithalen. Zij sloegen zich lakens om en gingen wandelen op een plaats, waar Jas passeren moest. Deze ging er echter niet voor door, maar begon de \"juffer\", die hij het eerst te pakken kreeg af te ranselen. De andere jongens sloegen toen op de vlucht","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"HOL002208","role":"variant","render":{"description":"In the evening, mistaking a stick with a newspaper on it for a witte juffer (white lady).","place":"Ochten","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210065","original":"Er moet een witte juffer gelopen hebben op het Zand (fruitteeltbedrijf) bij het witte hek (dit stond op de weg, die tussen twee kolken doorloopt. Keuken, hij was toen 18 jaar, ging eens met een kameraad naar Eldik (buurtschap) om een vriend te bezoeken. Deze bleek niet thuis. Op de dijk op de plaats waar beneden het witte hek stond, was een stok met krant er om gezet, als teken voor de castreur dat er \"keujes\" moesten gesneden worden. Janus stapte tegen deze stok aan, deze ging heen en weer, de kameraad beweerde, dat hij een witte juffer had gezien en was van dit idee, ook de volgende dag, niet af te brengen","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"HOL002604","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A white maiden who asks the way throws a hat full of money and disappears.","place":"Tiel","prov":"Gld.","year":1964,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210163","original":"Berend, den dakuil (een Van Uden) smeerde de daken van binnen aan met kalk, vandaar dat hij deze bijnaam kreeg. Eens liep Berend op de Grotebrugse grintweg bij de Twaalf Apostelen (straatje) toen een witte juffer hem de weg vroeg naar het veer. Berend zei haar die en nadat hij dit gedaan had, gooide zij hem de hoed vol met \"Berliner daolder\". Driemaal was Berend dit overkomen. Bij het veer gekomen wilde Berend haar bedanken, maar hij kreeg geen kans daartoe: zij was verdwenen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Gelderland an object was seen: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1962.","That card names an object. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"c5ba8ed615050990","accepted_hashes":["044e975dc1d42f65efe29fabaa04c285f01fa65c9a6c79f7204ab59664701fe6","3bfbcb3ee8e3a11ba389e8e814b3619d53eb46abcdcccbe696d80797c58e6155","b22e6a22100e4bf8ff8375c98dfa95a243ddb2419eae88e6430e77af739ae10a","bdd061bd9a16e3f32bc59ac53ca6112fc12afe835276ee2fff0fc5b2b1414f64","d91c124fb037487a9b6b226a1568e6b45330ba2dac07cb909f1fedc40ba309d2","ee5fecdb6f9cdc5dcdb72f2ce87f3415e2d53ad277bbd46d290226fe851ef5f3"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2226,"rank":0.7299,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CBOEK477","role":"member","render":{"description":"On a wager, a farmhand must show that he dares to throw the spit into the Witte Wieven (white women) pit. He throws it and challenges the witte wief (white woman), who chases him. The farmhand jumps over the lower half of the door, horse and all. The witte wief throws the spit, which sticks in the middle post of the door.","place":"Bathmen","prov":"Ov.","year":1892,"code":null,"initials":"J.V.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/39631","original":"In de buurtschap Loo, op het erve Noever ging men een weddenschap aan met een knecht, dat hij het spit niet durfde gooien in de Witte-wieven-kuul; deze bevond zich daar ergens in de buurt. Hij sprong te paard en joeg derwaarts, aldaar smeet hij het spit in de kuil met de woorden:\n\nWit wieven wit\nHier breng ik oe een spit\n(of: Wat heb ie'j op oe spit?)\n\nDaarop had het wit wief gezegd:\n\nA'j zoo lang wacht\nDak mien eene schoe toeknuppe\nEn de aander toerukke\nDan zal ie'j 't gebraad wezen.\n\nDe knecht rende toen in vliegenden vaart huiswaarts, achtervolgd door het wit wief en voor de achterdeur gekomen, was de bovendeur los en de onderdeur dicht, maar het paard was nogal vlug en sprong over de onderdeur. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LYST279","role":"member","render":{"description":"A farmhand brings the spit to the Witte Wieven (white women). One of them chases him. The farmhand just manages to flee into a house. The axe the Witte Wief (white woman) threw lands in the stiepel (doorpost). The Witte Wief could not run faster because she had trouble with one of her shoes.","place":"Tilligte","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":null,"initials":"B.R.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13623","original":"Door ouden wordt nog van de Wit Wieve verteld, die alleen kwaadaardig waren, wanneer ze getergd werden. Zo wordt verteld dat een boerenknecht eens het spit bracht naar de plaats, waar zij woonden. Hij werd door eene der witte wieve achtervolgd, doch hem niet kon inhalen, omdat ze in de haast maar een schoen had kunnen aantrekken. Toen de knecht het huis binnenvluchtte, wierp ze hem met een bijl achterna, die in de steil (deurpost) terecht kwam.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KEUNING005102","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A white ghost that floats over a gate into the field at night turns out to be a sheep.","place":"Drachten","prov":"Fr.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131150","original":"Sa ha se it yn Jistrum ek hast hâwn. Der laei njonken de hurde wei in brede mei gêrs bigroeide berm. En dêr kamen de stikken lân mei hikken op 'e daem op út. Nachts seach min hiel faek in wyt ding oer in hikke it lân yn sweven. Fansels, dat wie gjin goed spul. Fêst tsjoenderij. Mar hjir kaem ek ien, dy net oan sok spul leauwde en dy 't útmakke, dat it in drint (heideskiep) wie, dat fêst it gêrs yn de berm lekkerder foun as dat yn it lân.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELB_15_003","role":"member","render":{"description":"About the existence of witte wieven (white women) and the spit in the doorpost.","place":"Geesteren","prov":"Ov.","year":1979,"code":null,"initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128566","original":"H.E.: Van de witn wiew he’j doar wa mangs van heurd?\nVr.Vr.: Van de witn wiew is ok niks van woar.\nH.E.: Nee, mer te geet ok um t verhaal, he. Joa he’j hier nog zonnen beuld, zonnen witn wievnbeuld. Ne, nee, nee (door elkaar heen gepraat, ze zijn het met elkaar niet eens)\nVr. [Wolberink, Jan]: Wat hadn ze bie ouns ok zegd, oh jee no valt mie t kenneke in zee Dat stun nog moal vuur joarn in de Twentse kraant. Als ik t met ene schoen had vastgebondn, gevondn als de ander gebondn.\nA.Ve.: ... t spit nog in n stiel van n nienduur nog zitn.\nF.Ve.: t Spit brengn.","lang":"Twente dialect","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a ghost.","The card about Drachten belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.0967,"rank":0.8475,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"YPFOE070d","role":"card","render":{"description":"The narrator is heading home with a few friends. On the way they meet a white girl moving quickly. She floats towards a cottage. They go to investigate. Later an old man hanged himself, and people say it was connected with this. The minister is very sceptical about the story.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12149","original":"Wite juffers\nWat ik hjir yn 'e Westerein sels sjoen ha. Dat is no lyn, ik tink sa'n fiif-, seis-, sânenfyftich jier. Myn kammeraat en ik gyngen de jûntiid om in oere of alve stadichoan nei hûs ta. Doe troffen wy in pear jongelju en dy hâlden ús oan. De man sei: 'Sjoch, wat is dêr? Dêr is in famke midden yn 'e sûkerei. By it hûs dêre is it allegearre út en tsjuster, mar hoe kin dan sa'n wyt famke der yn 't lân weze?' Doe seach ik it ek. Ik sei: 'Dan moatte wy dêr ris even sjen'. Mar dat famke avensrarde tige hurd en wy koenen sjen, dat it net gie, mar dat it sweefde. It hie de grutte sawat fan in gewoan famke, en sniewyt. Ik sei: 'No, sille wy ris sjen? …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ018012","role":"sill","render":{"description":"Three white ladies, sisters, always haunt a haunted spot. Later that place was also said to be called the 'Susterwei'.","place":"Garyp","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20251","stain":"three"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST293","role":"card","render":{"description":"A road is known as a haunted road. In the evening and at night a white woman can be seen on it, with long, silky hair. Her dress is covered with feathers. Often in the morning some of these little feathers can be seen lying on the road. Her presence seems to have a fatal influence.","place":"Holten","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"G.J.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13638","original":"Het Witte Wief van de Friezeberg\nDe weg van Rijssen naar Enter is vooral bekend als de spookweg. Vroeger liep langs de eerste helft van die weg door een rij dennen ongeveer 4 meter breed een voetpad dat door de meeste voetgangers gezocht werd om van de schaduw op de anders zoo stoffige zonnige weg te genieten. 's Avonds zou zich daar echter geen sterveling wagen, want dit pad was bij avond en nacht de geliefde wandelplaats van een witte vrouw, door meer dan één gezien. Ze was een slanke vrouw met lang zijachtig haar. Haar wit gewaad was met glanzende veeren bezet en menigmaal kon men 's morgens van die witte veertjes zien liggen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"YPFOE070b","role":"card","render":{"description":"There was once a man who went with his dog cart from Hardegarijp to Bergum. A white figure travelled with him the whole way.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12147","original":"Wite juffers\nDer wie ris in man, dy reizge mei de hûnekarre de Simmerdyk del fan Hurdegaryp nei Burgum. It wie jûn en tige mistich. Hy siet yn 'e hûnekarre en njonken him siet in wite gestalte. De hiele tiid is dy njonken him meireizge, oan Burgum ta. Dy man hat in benaud oerke trochmakke.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"LYST223","role":"card","render":{"description":"Grote Kees was walking over a little bridge at midnight. Suddenly he could no longer move. Witte wieven (white women) float past him. Only when they had passed could he move again.","place":"Putten","prov":"Gld.","year":1937,"code":null,"initials":"A.W.v.G.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13487","original":"De \"Witte Wieven\" zijn hier in verhalen wel bekend. Van \"de groote Kees\" wordt verteld, dat hij ze gezien heeft. Toen hij een jonge kerel was, keerde hij eens tegen middernacht van een familiebezoek terug naar huis. Onderweg moest hij door een moerassige hei, de \"breistroet\", waar een bruggetje over een beek voerde. Midden op de brug gekomen, zag hij plotseling de witte wieven. Hij kon zich niet meer verroeren en drukte zich met de rug tegen de brugleuning. Langzaam zweefden ze nader en gingen rakelings langs hem heen over de brug. Na eenige tijd kon hij zich weer bewegen. Nat van 't zweet, \"an ieder haor hing 'n dropal\", kwam hij thuis. Ze zijn ook op de Staverense hei. Bovengenoemd persoon heeft het aldus aan een kennis van mij verteld.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"ENGELB_01_005","role":"card","render":{"description":"Men who go to the place where women have seen a wit wief (white woman) find a white sheet flapping there.","place":"Gammelke","prov":"Ov.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128373"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with G.","Garyp. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c2","object":"window","text":"Garyp"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c2","word":"three","stained":"c2"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P1","difficulty":0.7182,"rank":0.5495,"note":"All four name the same thing. That becomes the label. Don’t write ‘a beast’.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KUSTERS001702","role":"card","render":{"description":"A wreath in a bed, a sign of approaching death, cannot be pulled apart. A farmer suspects his farmhand of witchcraft, sends him to work elsewhere and throws the wreath into the baking oven. At once the farmhand is standing by the oven. After the wreath is burnt, the farmhand is freed from the devil.","place":"Nederweert","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"C.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46365","original":"Bij 'n boer was 'n krans in 't bed als teken van nabije dood. Zo'n krans was zo fijn gevlochten, dat men ze niet uiteen kon krijgen. De boer verdacht zijn knecht van die hekserij en stuurde hem voor werk naar de Peel wel 2 uur ver. Daarop stookte de boer zijn bakoven en gooide de krans daarin. Meteen stond de knecht voor hem en men moest hem met geweld tegenhouden anders was hij 't vuur in gegaan. Toen de krans verbrand was, zuchtte de knecht verlicht: \"nu ben ik gelukkig\" Hij was van de duivel bevrijd.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LINSSEN001002","role":"card","render":{"description":"When the wreaths that a farmhand has hung in a tree are burnt, the farmhand who had been sent away is suddenly back; release from the enchantment after the wreaths are burnt.","place":"Asenray","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208255","original":"Kransen in bomen. Een boerenknecht hield er eigenaardige gewoonten op na. In een boom nabij de boerderij hing hij kransen op, althans men meende dat hij dat deed, aangezien hij vaak met aandacht daarnaar keek. Men vond dit zeer vreemd en men zocht een gelegenheid om die kransen te verwijderen. Men stuurde hem met paard en wagen naar Sittard. Toen hij enige uren weg was haalde men de kransen uit de bomen en wierp ze in de \"bakoven\", die destijds bij vele boerderijen stond en diende om het eigen brood te bakken. Op hetzelfde ogenblik dat de kransen begonnen te branden stond de knecht op mysterieuze wijze voor de bakoven en wilde de kransen naspringen. Hij werd hiervan weerhouden door anderen die de oven stookten. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN002605","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand who turns into a black cat at midnight by means of a rim is released after the rim is burned.","place":"Baexem","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208342","original":"Volgens tweede verteller was er op Nelishof te Tungelroy een knecht die elke nacht tussen twaalf en een uur afwezig was. Door een raampje ging hij naar buiten. Hij klom dan op de schansenhoop en kwam er als kat af. De boer had hem bespied en gemerkt dat boven op de schansenhoop een velg lag van een karwiel. Die had de boer daar niet neergelegd en hij zocht verband tussen de spokerij (zwarte kat) en dat karwiel.\nDit zou hij vernietigen als de knecht afwezig was. Op zekere dag had hij hem met schapen naar Antwerpen gestuurd. Toen hij een dag weg was stak de boer zijn bakoven aan en wierp de velg erin.\nOp hetzelfde moment verscheen de knecht en wilde de oven in. Het gelukte slechts met drie man om hem daarvan te weerhouden. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LINSSEN003405","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand goes at night to a belt hidden in a tree; when the belt is thrown into the fire, the farmhand, who should be far away, is present.","place":"Horn","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208417","original":"V Een knecht van de Donk klaagde bij de boer dat zijn medeknecht er 's nachts vaak op uitging en zodoende zijn nachtrust stoorde. Men ging er eens op letten wat hij 's nachts uitvoerde. Men bespiedde hem. Op een nacht zag men dat hij naar Petite-Nak, een weiland, ging waar knotwilgen stonden. Bij een van deze knotwilgen bleef hij staan en reikte met zijn arm in de holle stam. De boer stuurde deze knecht op een morgen naar de Peel (Meyel) om turf. Intussen ging men naar de knotwilg en haalde daaruit een leren riem. De boer wilde die tijdens zijn afwezigheid verbranden, maar juist toen hij de riem in het vuur wilde gooien stond de knecht, die eigenlijk in Meyel moest zijn, in levenden lijve voor hem en wilde hem verhinderen de riem te verbranden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Read the four again. Look at what occurs in each of the four, not at what happens in them.","It is a profession.","Begins with F. 8 letters."],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"c5ba8ed615050990","accepted_hashes":["0c134a76b6695e2d465c76f4d99bed3b057ef79f1b9069c2023eed011759940f","37adc579cb0e2d0eccb1985e4a30a83124104ff1a5071c6e0ead771391cecb00","40eb9729775b0ae875595c7030099159bfe977ab930ce92ff95d6defa1daa669","47153aa5c08c2270d89443d91e7fde1308aafa4a1a0387382bb154a24d5146f9","5895cbd06a9f194e28b97f0bafdb1d5606db83e06f142f9b5def48465be09c4a","63d0ab73ea47dbffaffb3c9012796dc0c190ab81c26338f8870f44294f206f18","6fc2c97d55fdd3067bac235a5ee2e4e98f6dca5d4e58c288ece7212f922d251e","9f7d2c009eee9067a25b3e4b7f687bacfe45ba0d05c97564dbe98748b4688baf","ade8f4edf2f817796fca36e7bbb82edcca3fae4ee275097dd5cc1fc5eb33af73"]},"on_success":{"print_label":true,"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.0037,"rank":0.3841,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KOOIJMAN2574","role":"member","render":{"description":"In the old days there were people of whom it was said that they could turn into werewolves, change into a black dog.","place":"Spijk","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1964,"code":null,"initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128075","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ045113","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Witte wieven (white women) used to haunt a haunted spot.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24238","original":"Op dit ein fan 'e Folgerster loane spoeken froeger wite wiven.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1376","role":"member","render":{"description":"The werewolf was used to frighten small children.","place":"Werkendam","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/72899","original":"[De weerwolf:] Dat was onder de kleine kindertjes bangmakerij.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KOOIJMAN2124","role":"member","render":{"description":"A man is chased by a werewolf.","place":"Giessen","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/127468","original":"Mijn vader lachte daar zelf om. Maar hij heeft me eens verteld, er was een man, die er een op z'n rug kreeg bij het Koepeltje. Die plaats stond ongunstig bekend. Het spookte er zogenaamd altijd. Die man kwam thuis, helemaal onder het zweet, maar toen hij over de drempel van z'n huis was, was hij de weerwolf kwijt. Ik heb die man in mijn kinderjaren nog gekend.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Houtigehage belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.0602,"rank":0.5385,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"ENGELS001721","role":"door","render":{"description":"Man has to walk around with a werewolf for two days.","place":"Grashoek","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210547","original":"Weerwolven:\nIk heb eens horen vertellen van een man in Kessel, die twee dagen met een weerwolf op zijn rug moest lopen. Hij werd hem eindelijk kwijt, door hem tussen twee dicht bijeen staande bomen af te wringen. Hij had de klauwsporen op zijn borst staan.\n\nVerslag 50, Omzetting van de verhalen, verteld door Leonardus Kluijtmans, Helden, doorgegeven onder no. L291-17, op 26-12-1962. Van Nederl. versie in plaatselijk dialect. Helden, 4 nov. 1969\nIch heb èns huuëre vertèlle van enne mins in Kèèssel, dè twieë daag mèt te wèèrwolf hei motten drage. Hè woord öm kwiet, dor öm tössen twieë buim, die kort bei-ein sjtonge, van de rök te vringe. Later hei ’n de klauwsjpóre nag op zien boorst staon.","lang":"Standard Dutch; Limburgish","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST008","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every night at exactly twelve o'clock a farmhand takes a small hoop out of the lime tree. He hangs the hoop around his neck and turns into a werewolf. He roams about for a while and tears apart everything that comes near him. After that he becomes an ordinary person again. The farmer finds his behaviour strange and asks the priest for advice. The priest realises that the farmhand is a werewolf and advises the farmer to send the farmhand on an errand from which he can never be back home by midnight. On the agreed night the priest takes the hoop out of the tree at midnight. The farmhand is standing under that tree and sees everything. He flees and never comes back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0803","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13222","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen boerenknecht kroop 's nachts klokslag 12 uur in de lindenboom voor de boerderij. Boven in de boom hing voor gewone mensen onzichtbaar een hoepeltje. Dat hing de knecht om zijn hals. Als ie uit de boom geklauterd was, liep ie in de gedaante van een hond weg en verscheurde alles wat hem in de weg kwam. Als ie een tijd zo rondgelopen had, was ie weer gewoon mens. Na een tijd was het de boer, bij wie de weerwolf in dienst was, opgevallen, dat zijn knecht nacht op nacht weg was. Hij ging naar de pastoor en die had het zaakje meteen door. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"VODA_002_09","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of seven sons is a werewolf. Werewolves can also be recognised by their eyebrows that meet in the middle.","place":"Eindhoven","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1976,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/69626","original":"Als een vader zeven zonen had dan was een van die zeven zonen een weerwolf. ‘T is wel zo dat, bij een elkele vorige uitzending het had over de heksen, om een heks zo te kunnen herkennen, en zo herkent men ook de weerwolven. En in hoofdzaak kent men dan de weerwolven, want die moesten weer een teken van de duivel hebben, natuurlijk, dat [eh], samengegroeide wenkbrauwen hadden he. Mensen die samengegroeide wenkbrauwen hadden die waren voorbestemd om [om, om, om, om] weerwolf te zijn, he. En verder ter war, verder kon men dan, men kon dus eerst in [eh] weerwolf worden door een verbond te sluiten met de duivel en dan kregen ze doorlopende wenkbrauwen want dan kon de duivel ze herkennen.","lang":"Brabant dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An even number.","2 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c2","object":"door","n":2},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c3","c4","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":6,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.7338,"rank":0.8218,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ052212","role":"top","render":{"description":"On a piece of land a fellow on a white horse is sometimes seen. As suddenly as the rider appeared, he vanishes again.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0410","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25202","half":"top"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ118005","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The two lawyers can never leave the circle and keep haunting that spot. Since then the piece of land has been called 'Advocatenland' (Lawyers' Land).","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0410"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"VODA_002_13","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The second night she is woken by the shrieking of a ghost that takes money from the windowsill and sits down to count it. The next morning she tells her host and they find the ghost's money. The host offers the woman half, but she says he should give it to the poor. After that the ghost no longer returns.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"VODA_035_10","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Just before they fall asleep, they hear someone come out of the water at the front of the boat and step off again at the back. When they go to look, there are only some ripples and bubbles on the water.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"Voda_022_03","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"After her death she must remain on earth as punishment. A priest banishes her into a fen, where she must stay forever and lures pigs into the water.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0410"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ037108","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The man died and out of poverty the woman had to sell the buckles after all. But because of this the dead man could find no rest, and he appeared as a ghost to the woman and the children. The minister addressed the ghost and then saw to it that the buckles came back to the family. After that they never saw the apparition again.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"KEMP180","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The ghost counts the money it has hidden there in the wall and keeps teasing the sleeping man, but the soldier does not stir. The ghost disappears again. The next day the man takes the pot of money with him. The innkeeper is amazed that he survived the night. The ghost never returned. It is said that it was a man from the village who was very attached to his money.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"CJ052212","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"He is a ghost rider on a ghost horse. A castle used to stand at that spot. The ghost rider is the former lord of the castle. Later the rider is banished by exorcists to another piece of land. The narrator once saw the lord too: a reddish fellow with a pockmarked skin.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0410"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"JCOHEN50e","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"But at night she had to give way, and she walked to the door, where she slid back the bolts. \"Kroe — kroe —\" went the rusty sound. The granddaughter went to the door. \"Surely I locked the bolts?\" she thought. \"I'd better do it again!\" She locked the door again in the usual way. But invisible fingers seized her and the bolt she held in her hand was torn from her, so that she fled from this place where the dead woman still lingered.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"VODA_009_23","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"While prayers are belatedly said for the salvation of her soul, a number of sacks of potatoes are stolen from the barn.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"CJ023902","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He told an acquaintance that he had not seen the old woman but her skeleton with a cloth wrapped around it.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"CJ081006","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Then one night her mother suddenly stood before the bed. The woman was terrified and never again wished to see her mother.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"ENGELS001802","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"who advises putting new cattle into the stable backwards, and says that the mother-in-law practises witchcraft; a winnowing mill is seen turning by itself, and a black dog is seen.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The bottom piece mentions ‘horse’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0410. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c8"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c8"],"stack":["c1","c8"]},"found_card":{"card":"c8"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.4699,"rank":1.2439,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ101503","role":"member","render":{"description":"Mindert Slof [Tuinstra] was picking heather with his wife and son. It was foggy and they saw something floating over the heath. The father asked his son whether it floated or shuffled. When the son said it floated, they took to their heels.","place":"Drachtstercompagnie","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36965","original":"Der wenne yn 'e Houtigehage in sekere Mindert Slof (= Tuinstra). Hy en syn wiif en bern wienen skrobbermakkers.\nHja gongen altyd to heideteppen achter Ûrterp yn 'e Mesken. Op in kear wie hy dêr mei syn jonge. 't Waer wie hwat mistich. Doe seagen se oer de heide hwat sweven.\nDoe frege de âld man oan 'e jonge: \"Sweeft it of sloft it?\"\n\"It sweeft heit\", sei de jonge.\n\"Set dan sok\", sei de âld man. Hja naeiden hurd út.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEUNING004407","role":"member","render":{"description":"Fleeing from something that floats through the air.","place":"Drachtstercompagnie","prov":"Fr.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131104","original":"It wie yn it fean. G. roun dêr mei syn jonge. Doe seach G. hwat oer de bulten sweven. Hy warskouwe de jonge. \"Tink der om, astou hwat sweven sjochste, moast útnaeie, sa hurd astou kinste.\" Fuort dêr op rôp de jonge: \"Heit, dêr giet hwat troch de loft.\" En heit en soan fleagen nei hûs ta, boppe oer de swepen hinne.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ044801","role":"member","render":{"description":"A woman once saw something float over the houses. She did not know what it was; it was something ghostly.","place":"Drachtstercompagnie","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24195","original":"Doe't ik noch in jonge wie wenne der in frou yn Surhústerfean, dy seach hwat oer de wyk hinne sweven. Hwat it wie, wist se net, mar 't wie spûkerij.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ098702","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A little woman was walking outside one evening. Suddenly she saw something black. She asked it to come if it was of the Lord, and to go away if it was of Satan. It went away. The woman fled home, frightened to death.","place":"Noardburgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36489","original":"Hjir yn Burgumerheide wenne in âld-wyfke, dy wie by jountiid ris in kear bûtendoar, doe soe se nei hûs ta. Hja gong in smel reedtsje del en doe seach se dêr hwat. It wie hwat swarts. Hja koe net sjen hwat it wie, mar it forweegde en it makke har rare bang. Doe sei se: \"Is 't fan de Heare, kom ta my, en is 't fan 'e Satan, wyk fan my.\"\nIt gong fuort. Doe makke se hurd dat se thúskom, deabinaud.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Noardburgum belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.2143,"rank":0.7917,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"BOEKV147","role":"top","render":{"description":"A farmer lives in a haunted farmhouse. When an old soldier comes begging, the farmer asks whether he will keep watch.","place":"Uitdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1903,"code":"SINSAG 0401","initials":"C.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35028","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEMP173","role":"half","render":{"description":"Fortunately he knows that you must be bold with ghosts and never give them their way. He follows the ghost but refuses to carry out the tasks it gives him. The next day the craftsman has grey hair, but he is in possession of a treasure. From then on he can live off his wealth.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ015407","role":"half","render":{"description":"When she later goes to feed the pigs, the child's ghost keeps appearing. The child keeps putting its little hands on the pig trough.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ073804","role":"half","render":{"description":"Then Ruerd threatened to knock him down if he did not wait. The other then stopped. When Ruerd reached him, the other grabbed him several times and threw him over the trees. The next day they found him unconscious with all his ribs broken.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"BOEKV147","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"At midnight the soldier sees six ghosts pass by; high-ranking officers who dig a hole by the haystack with their sabres. The ghosts pull up a kettle of gold coins and hide it again. In the morning the soldier asks the farmhand to help him dig. By the haystack they find the kettle of gold and take it. At night the ghosts come to dig again, but find nothing and never return. The farmer is pleased and offers the soldier lodging and a reward. The soldier accepts the lodging, but by now he has enough money.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401","stain":"six"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ093904","role":"half","render":{"description":"He died in an accident with a horse and now his treasure lies there under the ground. The old man haunts the place and people are terrified. The old man keeps coming closer.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ082909","role":"half","render":{"description":"The man cannot bear it and fetches the minister. The minister says to the ghost: 'If you are of God, come to me; if you are of the devil, depart.' The ghost disappears and never comes back.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘farmer’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0401. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c5","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c5"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":6,"card":"c1","word":"six","stained":"c5"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
